cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Probing Compositional Question Difficulty in Language Model Representations"
abstract: >-
  Code for a study of whether a question's
  compositional difficulty is linearly decodable from a frozen instruction-tuned
  LLM's hidden states of the question itself, before any answer is produced.
  Three models (Qwen2.5-32B, Mistral-24B, Gemma-27B) are crossed with three
  multi-hop QA benchmarks (2WikiMultiHopQA, HotpotQA, MuSiQue) at 300 questions
  per class.
